(6584591, 980984, 49018, '<td valign="top">This one would have been an ideal candidate for HDR, I think, or simply for shooting raw and underexposing a bit, so to receover the brightness in postprocessing. The range seems to be too large,thus clipping detail and colors in the highlights, which spoils it a bit. Also, a much lower angle, if possible with the camera at water level, would have put more of the upper scene in the reflection, enhancing the sense of perspective. The scene in itself is lovely.</td>', 'This one would have been an ideal candidate for HDR, I think, or simply for shooting raw and underexposing a bit, so to receover the brightness in postprocessing. The range seems to be too large,thus clipping detail and colors in the highlights, which spoils it a bit. Also, a much lower angle, if possible with the camera at water level, would have put more of the upper scene in the reflection, enhancing the sense of perspective. The scene in itself is lovely.', '2011-11-04 05:41:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584593, 980719, 49018, '<td valign="top">This would have worked well in HDR I think.</td>', 'This would have worked well in HDR I think.', '2011-11-04 05:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584599, 979801, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like this. I remember a friend putting a piece of, uhh, masking tape were the water sprouts from, to divert the water so to make a similar shot more symmetrical :)</td>', 'I like this. I remember a friend putting a piece of, uhh, masking tape were the water sprouts from, to divert the water so to make a similar shot more symmetrical :)', '2011-11-04 05:46:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584608, 979988, 49018, '<td valign="top">Possibly, a lower angle would have worked better (sneakily, maybe even arranging the leaves in a symmetrical pattern or path, given the bridge seems to end on a bunch of leaves). I find fascinating that the bridge seems to lead, well, nowhere. Chromatically, maybe it would work better with a less pronounced green dominant.</td>', 'Possibly, a lower angle would have worked better (sneakily, maybe even arranging the leaves in a symmetrical pattern or path, given the bridge seems to end on a bunch of leaves). I find fascinating that the bridge seems to lead, well, nowhere. Chromatically, maybe it would work better with a less pronounced green dominant.', '2011-11-04 05:54:02.000000', NULL, 0),
