(6584790, 980855, 49018, '<td valign="top">On this one, I would have cranked up the ISO so to get more DOF. Neatimage, noiseninja, topaz and the like are quite good at preserving detail in postprocessing while removing noise, and downsizing for submission will anyway produce a sharper picture than full size. Also, maybe an half stop underexposure, maybe more, could have been restored easily in postprocessing while granting you  bit faster shutter speed or narrower aperture.</td>', 'On this one, I would have cranked up the ISO so to get more DOF. Neatimage, noiseninja, topaz and the like are quite good at preserving detail in postprocessing while removing noise, and downsizing for submission will anyway produce a sharper picture than full size. Also, maybe an half stop underexposure, maybe more, could have been restored easily in postprocessing while granting you  bit faster shutter speed or narrower aperture.', '2011-11-04 09:09:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584791, 980868, 12611, '<td valign="top">What strikes me is the texture of the steps, white and flowing, and then the plateau of stone. Another great shot.</td>', 'What strikes me is the texture of the steps, white and flowing, and then the plateau of stone. Another great shot.', '2011-11-04 09:11:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584795, 980912, 121949, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful image Christophe. The lengths you go to pursue a shot still amazes me. Congrats!</td>', 'Very beautiful image Christophe. The lengths you go to pursue a shot still amazes me. Congrats!', '2011-11-04 09:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6584798, 980683, 49018, '<td valign="top">More recovery of the highlights would have helped too, if possible and if your converter allows for it, given it was shot in raw.  Or just underexponsing a bit and lift shadows up in postprocessing. And further straightening.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-11-04 09:23:10.</i></td>', 'More recovery of the highlights would have helped too, if possible and if your converter allows for it, given it was shot in raw.  Or just underexponsing a bit and lift shadows up in postprocessing. And further straightening.', '2011-11-04 09:21:59.000000', '2011-11-04 09:23:10.000000', 0),
(6584813, 980597, 104230, '<td valign="top">Wonderful image.  Great placement of her head, lighting, focus, and DOF. That knot of hair, plus the lights in it, plus the other lit part of her hair for me provide the sense of a "pivot" point, around which the rest of her could spin, or be spun, if one wished.  Appropriate for someone I assume is a ballerina or dancer!</td>', 'Wonderful image.  Great placement of her head, lighting, focus, and DOF. That knot of hair, plus the lights in it, plus the other lit part of her hair for me provide the sense of a "pivot" point, around which the rest of her could spin, or be spun, if one wished.  Appropriate for someone I assume is a ballerina or dancer!', '2011-11-04 09:36:47.000000', NULL, 0),
